course: dictionary
lesson: 8930
title: Signalling: giving a sign
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Signalling means giving a sign, sound or light to send a message. A cyclist signalling left puts out one arm to tell other road users which way she will turn.
explain: Look at «Dark clouds are signalling rain.» Clouds cannot wave an arm, so here signalling means showing that something is about to happen. The dark clouds are a sign that rain is coming.
explain: Signalling can also be a noun for a whole system of signals, such as «railway signalling» or «cell signalling». When you meet a new word, ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Signalling is the present form of the verb «signal», which means to give a sign, sound or light to send a message.
fact: «Signalling» can also mean showing that something is happening, as in «Dark clouds are signalling rain.»
fact: «Signalling» as a noun means a system of signals, as in «railway signalling».
fact: «A signal shows red when a train is in the section ahead.» Drivers and trains use signals to stay safe.
fact: «Hand signals» are signs made with the hands, such as a cyclist putting out an arm before turning.
exercise: «Chameleons change colour mainly for mood, signalling and temperature.» In this sentence, what does signalling mean? | *Giving messages to other chameleons | Sleeping in the sun | Growing a longer tail | Counting the spots on its skin
exercise: «Dark clouds are signalling rain.» What are the clouds showing? | Rain has already stopped | The clouds are sending a phone call | The clouds are made of snow | *Rain is about to come
exercise: A cyclist puts out one arm before turning. What is she doing? | Changing gears | *Signalling which way she will turn | Waving hello to a friend | Stopping the bike with her hands
test: «Modern signalling can stop a train automatically if it passes a red signal.» What is railway signalling here? | A ticket for the journey | A type of train engine | A bird that sits on the tracks | *A system of signals that keeps trains safe
test: «Male ring-tailed lemurs wave their tails at rivals; the tail is used for balance and signalling.» What is the lemur's tail used for? | Keeping the lemur warm at night | Swimming in rivers | Grabbing food from trees | *Balance and giving signals
exam: «Chameleons change colour for mood, signalling and temperature.» Which word is a synonym that shows giving a message? | colour | temperature | *signalling | mood
